er.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sin x \\cos x + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556254} {:answer/id #uuid "99b86bbc-42d4-5a73-bfe8-0b81a4a7c8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sin x \\cos x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99b86bbc-42d4-5a73-bfe8-0b81a4a7c8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sin x \\cos x - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556257} :answer-field/id #uuid "b753164c-0e5a-5ef8-a3fb-a69c038ce571" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fc06fa2c-e4ba-5f20-956b-c01b1e7bae0d" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\sin x(3\\cos x-2\\sin x)+\\cos x(3\\sin x-2\\cos x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\sin x(3\\cos x-2\\sin x)+\\cos x(3\\sin x-2\\cos x) = 3\\sin x\\cos x-2\\sin^{2}x+3\\sin x\\cos x-2\\cos^{2}x\n$$\n\nNext, we group the $\\sin^2 x$ and $\\cos^2 x$ terms.\n\n$$\n3\\sin x\\cos x-2\\sin^{2}x+3\\sin x\\cos x-2\\cos^{2}x = 6\\sin x\\cos x-2(\\sin^{2}x+\\cos^{2}x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^2{x}+\\cos^2{x}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n6\\sin x\\cos x-2(\\sin^{2}x+\\cos^{2}x) = 6 \\sin x \\cos x - 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin x(3\\cos x-2\\sin x)+\\cos x(3\\sin x-2\\cos x) = 6 \\sin x \\cos x - 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24ee5f71-37f2-50d6-ae8a-9bfa2a3e68bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{0}^{r}r^{2} z^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556293} {:answer/id #uuid "4e49c3a3-9740-5bef-9bdc-6a51c7364c8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{17}}^{2 \\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{0}^{r}r z^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556304} {:answer/id #uuid "8cdbc979-1803-56f6-b7a0-c904c039ff8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{0}^{12}r z^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556320} {:answer/id #uuid "9349e73f-aef8-59e0-a523-0ddc41b66c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{0}^{12}r^{2} z^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556321} {:answer/id #uuid "b16ff172-8fbe-5547-98e0-17218c4e502c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{17}}^{2 \\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{0}^{12}r^{2} z^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9349e73f-aef8-59e0-a523-0ddc41b66c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{0}^{12}r^{2} z^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556321} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a37a2e4-2236-5089-9702-0aa3e56fadda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556295}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c4f39f6-c3b9-5ce0-9e72-9d922968c0ed" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=17$ between the surfaces $z=0$ and $z=12.$ Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/99/994f3537bf54a849e6a725c4c692a2326266d8065a742b1988308c793708827f.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{17}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=12.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{17},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\\,0\\le z\\le 12\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{z}^{2}\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}r{z}^{2}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{0}^{12}{r}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b9a55a9-e21c-5f6b-83a7-1697dde3f5a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4}r^{4} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556315} {:answer/id #uuid "bcafc06b-d37c-56be-b7c8-ed39af45d2c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556333} {:answer/id #uuid "bee5f666-1739-5060-b52a-3a618de550f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556334} {:answer/id #uuid "c153d2dc-77a3-5d5b-840c-6705fe6d4796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556336} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb3cbb3-d693-5101-819b-f5167b411aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c153d2dc-77a3-5d5b-840c-6705fe6d4796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556336} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c700b53-099b-567b-adf9-63c54f069d82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "37475e2f-873b-54fd-b9a9-28a66b2df1fd" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder $x^2+y^2=5$ for $x\\le 0$ and $y\\ge 0$, between the surfaces $z=x$ and $z=y^{2} + 4$. Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates.\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/3e/3e51a479b8fe2a00f7b51a8613fe2cb6a45d790d737637c31b7858766e0491ff.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-quarter of a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{5}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=x=r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=y^{2} + 4=r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta,z):0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{5},\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\pi,r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\le z\\le r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V&=\\iiint_\\Delta z((r\\cos\\theta)^2-(r\\sin\\theta)^2)\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta rz(r^2\\cos^2\\theta-r^2\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z\\cos(2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &={\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ebcc17a-019e-5c17-8bea-7b8844187a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556289} {:answer/id #uuid "12dbab12-164b-5680-94f9-924300098671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556290} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2fdac7-0129-5de8-a676-0df12f29a289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556318} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b96017-32cb-5f0a-9af2-8b846950d5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{4} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556327} {:answer/id #uuid "f68a34f1-2003-56dd-8559-7af6896e3609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f2fdac7-0129-5de8-a676-0df12f29a289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556318} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9eba1e2-1e2c-5034-83ba-ea01a4fdfe65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4236bbd5-5775-5328-8a6a-2b03d6b4100f" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder $x^2+y^2=4$ for $x\\le 0$ and $y\\ge 0$, between the surfaces $z=x$ and $z=y^{2} + 12$. Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates.\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/d8/d8c1c025e6e8992826d8629a129d83906a4af3c566d44dbb25fcdf7dca9df64d.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-quarter of a right vertical cylinder of radius $2$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=x=r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=y^{2} + 12=r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta,z):0\\le r\\le 2,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\pi,r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\le z\\le r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V&=\\iiint_\\Delta z((r\\cos\\theta)^2-(r\\sin\\theta)^2)\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta rz(r^2\\cos^2\\theta-r^2\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z\\cos(2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &={\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 12}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f450272-2e20-535b-a3da-b40d2daea374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{30}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}r^{4} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556313} {:answer/id #uuid "a12e1c95-2e9a-580a-a1e0-2bf00ccfdae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{30}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556325} {:answer/id #uuid "afe542a2-3272-58b9-8f21-5b1f9701a74a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{30}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556328} {:answer/id #uuid "c086bb8a-9cd2-5cc7-a826-874be4317f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{30}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556335} {:answer/id #uuid "f4534025-7c2f-50e3-8205-350588ad8911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{30}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}r^{2} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c086bb8a-9cd2-5cc7-a826-874be4317f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{30}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556335} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3d11861-12d7-5f03-98fc-62e81a2cb6d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "45e354dd-5085-53a8-8e15-e1130241495c" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder $x^2+y^2=30$ for $x\\le 0$ and $y\\ge 0$, between the surfaces $z=x$ and $z=y^{2} + 1$. Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates.\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/07/07f1c4ca9e71cac2149bee4c4ae2e4f506f280b580ff0a391229f7e1624f2119.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-quarter of a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{30}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=x=r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=y^{2} + 1=r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta,z):0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{30},\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le\\theta\\le \\pi,r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\le z\\le r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R z \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}V&=\\iiint_\\Delta z((r\\cos\\theta)^2-(r\\sin\\theta)^2)\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta rz(r^2\\cos^2\\theta-r^2\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\iiint_\\Delta r^3z\\cos(2\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &={\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{30}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}r^{3} z \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f055e72-6e2d-5f80-9979-e2072e2c4ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r^{2} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556298} {:answer/id #uuid "6c764d73-7539-571d-815d-01116fae9260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r^{3} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556311} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9d16bc-af7d-530a-bd41-8aad14966abc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r^{3} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556323} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fedc8f-f785-58f5-8e87-afcb82a70dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r^{3} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556331} {:answer/id #uuid "ced3c7d7-0a5d-5016-a660-b61a71702f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r^{2} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5fedc8f-f785-58f5-8e87-afcb82a70dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}^{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r^{3} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556331} :answer-field/id #uuid "b816efcf-ee31-5d4d-b5a0-f4d15dfc9f02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e3cd9a6-4a6e-5025-b51b-7ed39764e4aa" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=17$ for $x\\le 0,$ between the surfaces $z=x$ and $z={y}^{2}.$ Express the following triple integral in cylindrical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/24/249116dd79140b8e49d64902c46a3f0bc7c6411c9f8e7129faf38c64e7cc859e.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-half of a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{17}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z={y}^{2}={r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{17},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta <\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\,r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le z\\le {r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}-(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}r({r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{17}}{\\int }_{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }^{{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
